{{also|sõrmi}}
==Finnish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fi|fiu-fin-pro|*sormi}}, from {{inh|fi|fiu-pro|*sorme}}. Cognates include {{cog|et|sõrm}}, {{cog|se|suorbma}} and {{cog|myv|сур}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{hyphenation|sor|mi|lang=fi}}
* {{IPA|/ˈsormi/|lang=fi}}

===Noun===
{{head|fi|noun}}

# {{lb|fi|anatomy}} [[finger]] {{gloss|one of the five extremities of the hand}}
#: {{ux|fi|Ihmiskädessä on viisi sormea: [[peukalo]], [[etusormi]], [[keskisormi]], [[nimetön]] ja [[pikkusormi]].|The human hand has five fingers: the thumb, the forefinger, the middle finger, the ring finger and the little finger.}}
# finger {{gloss|extremity of an animal's forelimb, which resembles human finger}}
# finger {{gloss|any object which resembles a finger, such as a part of a mechanical device}}

